Encoding: UTF-8
Description: Coordinated-effects models for merger analysis built on the
    structural demand and cost calibration infrastructure provided by the
    'antitrust' package. Implements the price leadership equilibrium (PLE)
    model of coordinated conduct -- a coordinating coalition that prices
    above Bertrand levels subject to incentive-compatibility constraints,
    with a competitive fringe that best-responds -- following Mansley,
    Miller, Sheu & Weinberg (2023). Also implements Grim Trigger
    sustainability analysis for evaluating whether a coalition of firms
    playing Bertrand can sustain collusive pricing under a repeated game.
